&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Group of Seven &lt;/strong&gt;is an &lt;strong&gt;inter-governmental political forum &lt;/strong&gt;consisting of &lt;strong&gt;Canada&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;France&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Germany&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Italy&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Japan&lt;/strong&gt;, the &lt;strong&gt;United Kingdom&lt;/strong&gt;, and the &lt;strong&gt;United States&lt;/strong&gt;. In addition, the &lt;strong&gt;European Union &lt;/strong&gt;is a &lt;strong&gt;&amp;#39;non-enumerated member&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;G7 provides global leadership &lt;/strong&gt;and &lt;strong&gt;plays a powerful catalyst role &lt;/strong&gt;on issues that are later taken up by other &lt;strong&gt;fora &lt;/strong&gt;with &lt;strong&gt;broader global and regional membership&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;G7 brings together &lt;/strong&gt;the &lt;strong&gt;world&amp;#39;s advanced economies &lt;/strong&gt;to &lt;strong&gt;influence global trends &lt;/strong&gt;and &lt;strong&gt;tackle pervasive &lt;/strong&gt;and &lt;strong&gt;crosscutting issues&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;G7 is an organized group &lt;/strong&gt;of &lt;strong&gt;seven countries &lt;/strong&gt;that are &lt;strong&gt;regarded &lt;/strong&gt;as some of the &lt;strong&gt;world&amp;#39;s largest &amp;#39;advanced&amp;#39; economies &lt;/strong&gt;that are &lt;strong&gt;highly positioned in global trade &lt;/strong&gt;and the &lt;strong&gt;international financial system&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Leaders of the Group of Seven &lt;/strong&gt;(G7), who met in &lt;strong&gt;Elmau&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Germany&lt;/strong&gt;, on &lt;strong&gt;26-28 June 2022&lt;/strong&gt;, were joined by the Leaders of &lt;strong&gt;Argentina&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;India&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Indonesia&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Senegal&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;South Africa&lt;/strong&gt;, as well as &lt;strong&gt;Ukraine&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The choice of &lt;strong&gt;Taormina &lt;/strong&gt;as the &lt;strong&gt;headquarters &lt;/strong&gt;of the &lt;strong&gt;G7 &lt;/strong&gt;was &lt;strong&gt;announced &lt;/strong&gt;by the then &lt;strong&gt;Prime Minister Matteo Renzi on 4 July 2016&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

