&lt;p dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The indirect speech of the given sentence is&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Anne said that in the following week she had her first skating lesson.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border=&quot;1&quot; cellpadding=&quot;0&quot; cellspacing=&quot;0&quot; style=&quot; width: 350px;&quot; width=&quot;350&quot;&gt;
	&lt;tbody&gt;
		&lt;tr&gt;
			&lt;td&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Anne said&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Next week I have my first skating lesson.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Reporting clause&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Reported speech&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul style=&quot;&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;When the reporting speech is in&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;present perfect tense&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;then all the speech&amp;nbsp;Changes to&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;past perfect tense&lt;/span&gt;.

	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;have-----had&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Said&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;of the reporting verb remains the same.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Replace&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;comma (,) and inverted commas (&amp;quot; &amp;quot;)&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;with the conjunction &amp;#39;&lt;b&gt;that&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#39;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;I(first person)&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;of the Reported Speech changed according to the subject of the Reporting clause(Sh&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Change &lt;strong&gt;Next week&lt;/strong&gt; into&lt;strong&gt; the following week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;​So, the final sentence is:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;​&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Anne said that in the following week she had her first skating lesson.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;What is Direct &amp;amp; Indirect Speech?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul style=&quot;&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Direct speech&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;ndash; reporting the message of the speaker in the exact words as spoken by him.&lt;/div&gt;

	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Direct speech example&lt;/span&gt;: Maya said, &amp;quot;I am busy now&amp;quot;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Indirect speech&lt;/span&gt;: reporting the message of the speaker in our own words&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Indirect speech example&lt;/span&gt;: Maya said that she was busy then.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Given&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Side of square increased by 40%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Formula used&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Percentage increased = (change in area/original area) &amp;times; 100&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calculation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;let the side of square is 100 units&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;side increased by 40%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Original area of square = 100&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; 100&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;10000 sq units&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;New area of square = 140&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; 140&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;19600&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Change in area = 19600 - 10,000&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;9600&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Area increased by = (9600/10000)&amp;nbsp;&amp;times; 100&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;96%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;there4; Area of square increased by 96%.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

