&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;Omniscient&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Let&amp;#39;s see the meanings of the given words-
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experienced-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;having gained knowledge or skill in a particular field over time.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Omniscient-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;knowing everything.(सर्वज्ञ)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Invincible-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;too powerful to be defeated or overcome.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Na&amp;iuml;ve&lt;/span&gt;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;(of a person or action) showing a lack of experience, wisdom, or judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Hence, according to the meanings of the given words, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;Option 2 i.e. Omniscient.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;&amp;#39;The teacher told Asif to go and wash his hands.&amp;#39;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul style=&quot;&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The given sentence is in&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Direct Speech.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;As per the question we have to change it into&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Indirect&amp;nbsp;Speech.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The process of transformation is as follows:
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;The given sentence is an example of an&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;imperative&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;sentence&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Let&amp;#39;s look at the rules of transformation:&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;While changing the narration of an &lt;strong&gt;imperative sentence&lt;/strong&gt;, we need to follow the given steps:
		&lt;ul&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;The notion of the given sentence is &amp;#39;&lt;strong&gt;suggestion&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;#39;.&lt;/li&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;The conjunction &amp;#39;&lt;strong&gt;to&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;#39; should be used in place of&lt;strong&gt; a comma &lt;/strong&gt;(,) and&lt;strong&gt; inverted commas &lt;/strong&gt;(&amp;ldquo; &amp;rdquo;). &amp;#39;&lt;strong&gt;said&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;#39; will be changed into &amp;#39;&lt;strong&gt;told&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;#39;.&lt;/li&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;&amp;#39;&lt;strong&gt;to&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;#39; is followed by &amp;#39;&lt;strong&gt;V&lt;sub&gt;1&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;#39;.&lt;/li&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;&amp;#39;&lt;strong&gt;your&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;#39; will be changed into &amp;#39;&lt;strong&gt;his&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;#39; because &lt;strong&gt;second-person pronouns&lt;/strong&gt; are changed according to the &lt;strong&gt;object&lt;/strong&gt; of the &lt;strong&gt;reporting verb.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Example:&lt;/em&gt;
			&lt;ul&gt;
				&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;The queen said to his servant, &amp;quot;Cook me some delicious food today.&amp;quot; (Direct Speech)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
				&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;The queen ordered his servant to cook her some delicious food that day. (Indirect Speech)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
				&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
			&lt;/ul&gt;
			&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ul&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Correct Sentence:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;i&gt;The teacher told Asif to go and wash his hands.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;The logic followed here is:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;Prasad ranked eleventh from the top and twenty fourth from the bottom among those who had passed in the mid-term examination in a class.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;This means that the total number of students who passed the examination can be calculated by adding Prasad&amp;#39;s rank from the top and the bottom and then subtracting 1 (since Prasad is counted twice).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;Total number of students who passed = 11 + 24 - 1 = 34.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;Additionally, four students had failed in the mid-term examination.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;Therefore, the total number of students in the class = Total number of students who passed + Number of students who failed&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;= 34 + 4&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;= 38.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;Hence, the correct answer is &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;Option 4&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

