&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Given:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A man bought a number of apples at 5 for ₹50.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;He bought an equal number of apples at 6 for ₹50.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;He sells them at 11 for ₹100.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Formula Used:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cost Price (CP) = Total Cost / Total Number of Apples&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Selling Price (SP) = Total Selling Price / Total Number of Apples&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Profit or Loss Percentage = ((SP - CP) / CP) &amp;times; 100&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calculation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let the number of apples bought in each case be x.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cost for first set of apples: 5 apples for ₹50&lt;br /&gt;
Cost for x apples = (50/5) &amp;times; x = 10x&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cost for second set of apples: 6 apples for ₹50&lt;br /&gt;
Cost for x apples = (50/6) &amp;times; x = 8.33x&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Total Cost Price (CP) = 10x + 8.33x&lt;br /&gt;
CP = 18.33x&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Total apples bought = x + x = 2x&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Selling Price for 11 apples = ₹100&lt;br /&gt;
Selling Price for 1 apple = 100 / 11&lt;br /&gt;
Selling Price for 2x apples = 2x &amp;times; (100 / 11)&lt;br /&gt;
SP = (200x / 11)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Profit or Loss Percentage = ((SP - CP) / CP) &amp;times; 100&lt;br /&gt;
Profit or Loss Percentage = (((200x / 11) - 18.33x) / 18.33x) &amp;times; 100&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; Profit or Loss Percentage = (((200 / 11) - 18.33) / 18.33) &amp;times; 100&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; Profit or Loss Percentage = ((18.18 - 18.33) / 18.33) &amp;times; 100&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; Profit or Loss Percentage = (-0.15 / 18.33) &amp;times; 100&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; Profit or Loss Percentage = -0.818% = 100/121%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The man incurs a loss of (100 / 121)%.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

