&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The correct answer is&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#39;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;My car was stolen&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;.​&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul style=&quot;&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The given sentence is in&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Active Voice.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;As per the given question we have to change it into&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Passive Voice.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The structure of the given sentence is as follows:
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Subject + V2 + Object. (Active Voice)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Subject (objective case)+ was/were + V3 + Object (subjective case). (Passive Voice)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Example:&lt;/span&gt;
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Their cousin showed them some rare photographs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;(Active Voice)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;They were shown some rare photographs by their cousin.&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;(Passive Voice)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;The subject&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;of the given sentence is&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;#39;Someone&amp;#39;.​​&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;The object&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;of the given sentence is&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;#39;My car&amp;#39;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;The subject&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;will be put in place of&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;the object&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;and&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;the object&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;will be put in place of&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;the subject.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;And&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;#39;stole&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;will be changed into&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;#39;was&amp;nbsp;stolen&amp;#39;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;quot;Car&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;is a singular subject&amp;nbsp;so we must&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;quot;was&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;with it.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Therefore, as per the points mentioned above, we find that the correct answer is&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Option 4.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
	​&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Correct sentence&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;My car was stolen.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Given:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;In an examination, 52% of candidates failed in English and 42% failed in Mathematics and 17% of candidates failed in both English and Mathematics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Formula Used:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;math-tex&quot;&gt;\(n(M\cup E)\)&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;= n(M) + n(E) -&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;math-tex&quot;&gt;\(n(M\cap E)\)&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calculation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;According to the question,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;52% of candidates failed in English and 42% failed in Mathematics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;n(M) = 42% and&amp;nbsp;n(E) = 52%.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;17% of candidates failed in both English and Mathematics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;math-tex&quot;&gt;\(n(M\cap E)\)&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;= 17%.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Total candidates failed in both subjects&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;math-tex&quot;&gt;\(n(M \cup E)\)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;​&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;​&lt;/span&gt;​&amp;nbsp;&lt;span&gt;=&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;n(M) + n(E) - ​​&lt;span class=&quot;math-tex&quot;&gt;\(n(M \cap E)\)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr; ​&lt;span class=&quot;math-tex&quot;&gt;\(n(M \cup E)\)&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;= 42 + 52 - 17&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;rArr;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;math-tex&quot;&gt;\(n(M \cup E)\)&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;= 77%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;there4; The percentage of candidates who passed in both subjects = 100 - 77 = 23%.&lt;/p&gt;

