en.value:
&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is &amp;#39;&lt;strong&gt;Apart&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;#39;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Let&amp;#39;s go through the meanings of the words and then select the appropriate &lt;strong&gt;antonym&lt;/strong&gt; for &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;together&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot;:

	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apart&lt;/strong&gt; (अलग) - separated by a distance in time or space; not close to each other.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;United&lt;/strong&gt; (एकत्र) - joined together politically or for a common purpose; in agreement or harmony.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Freight&lt;/strong&gt; (सामान) - goods transported by truck, train, ship, or aircraft; cargo.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engulf&lt;/strong&gt; (लपेटना) - (verb) to completely surround or cover something; to immerse or swallow up.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Among these options, the most appropriate &lt;strong&gt;antonym for &amp;quot;together&amp;quot; is: Apart&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Explanation:&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;Together&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot; means in proximity or close association with each other, while &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;apart&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot; means separated or distant from each other. They are direct opposites in terms of spatial or temporal relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sentence using the correct option:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;After spending several years abroad, the siblings decided to live &lt;strong&gt;apart&lt;/strong&gt;, pursuing their individual dreams and aspirations.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;In this sentence, &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;apart&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;quot; is the &lt;strong&gt;antonym&lt;/strong&gt; of &amp;quot;&lt;strong&gt;together&lt;/strong&gt;,&amp;quot; &lt;strong&gt;indicating the opposite state of being close or united.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calculation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The percentage of students in Std. 6 and Std. 9&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Std. 6: 25%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Std. 9: 18%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Total: 25% + 18% = 43%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The percentage of students in Std. 10&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Std. 10: 15%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The difference between the two percentages = 43% - 15% = 28%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Percentage increase = 28/15&amp;nbsp;x 100% = 186.66%&amp;nbsp;&amp;asymp; 187%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;there4; Option (3) is the correct answer.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

hn.value:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;गणना&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;कक्षा 6 और कक्षा 9 में विद्यार्थियों&amp;nbsp;का प्रतिशत&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;कक्षा 6&lt;/span&gt;: 25%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;कक्षा 9&lt;/span&gt;: 18%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;कुल: 25% + 18% = 43%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;कक्षा 10 में विद्यार्थियों&amp;nbsp;का प्रतिशत&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;कक्षा 10&lt;/span&gt;: 15%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;दोनों प्रतिशत के बीच का अंतर = 43% - 15% = 28%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;प्रतिशत वृद्धि = 28/15&amp;nbsp;x 100% = 186.66%&amp;nbsp;&amp;asymp; 187%&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;there4; सही उत्तर &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(33, 37, 41);&quot;&gt;विकल्प (3)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;है।&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

en.value:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Given:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The total number of boys in Std. 8 is &amp;quot;x&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The total number of boys in Std. 9 is &amp;ldquo;x + 40&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;

